  "description": "Go vs Bun identity provider services head-to-head under identical k6 load.",
  "editable": true,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "id": null,
  "links": [],
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 3,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 200,
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "## Reading this dashboard\n\n**Go = blue. Bun = orange.** Lower latency, lower errors, higher RPS = better.\n\n- **Row 1** Current state at a glance (mean over the selected time range).\n- **Row 2** Latency per endpoint — solid p50, line p95, dashed p99. Both services overlaid per chart.\n- **Row 3** Errors and throughput over time.\n- **Row 4** Whole user journeys (flow durations).\n- **Row 5** App-side CPU/RAM/GC (collapsed by default).\n- **Row 6** k6 load generator health (collapsed).\n\nFilter top: **Scenario** (smoke/load/stress/soak). Time range top-right."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "id": 100,
      "title": "1 — Headline (average over selected range)",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 3
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
